                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b2c9d50d-cb33-4dbf-9d68-601592d19113",
                        "source_entry_id": "49846f81-265f-3a4a-92d9-f49dd9f38bdf",
                        "source_sense_id": "413c2e51-26a3-3540-b479-ba724c2637d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "transphobia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "transphobia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd7247e0-6fd2-3449-bb3d-f0f66f6311d1",
                                        "entry_id": "84ac2ba0-b3bd-3378-a3a6-bf5174e55c59",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hatred or fear of, or prejudice against, transgender and transsexual people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bb858c4-fa9a-41e5-890e-c5d0420a2162",
                                                "sense_id": "fd7247e0-6fd2-3449-bb3d-f0f66f6311d1",
                                                "text": "It is not really a debate about privacy and personal safety versus politics, so much as an impulse towards pride and a rejection of internalized transphobia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "418557e3-bb9e-4da5-872b-af1c0485420c",
                                                "sense_id": "fd7247e0-6fd2-3449-bb3d-f0f66f6311d1",
                                                "text": "In this case, transphobia is represented in Pollock's terms as both the \"condition and the effect\" of Cameron's social existence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf4d39d4-1922-3fd4-bcef-60d11145036c",
                                        "entry_id": "84ac2ba0-b3bd-3378-a3a6-bf5174e55c59",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The preference of pairs of high-trans effect soft ligands to avoid being mutually trans by becoming cis and having other low-trans effect hard ligands trans to themselves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da0ededb-4538-4545-a61c-508780a90132",
                                                "sense_id": "bf4d39d4-1922-3fd4-bcef-60d11145036c",
                                                "text": "This unusual reactivity and the selectivity observed can be explained as a consequence of the high transphobia of aryl and P-donor ligands […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0183b877-0859-4453-a14d-7731fadf7b4b",
                                                "sense_id": "bf4d39d4-1922-3fd4-bcef-60d11145036c",
                                                "text": "The reactions of trans-[Pt(Mef)Br(PPh₃)₂] with AgBF₄ and Ph₃ECHC(O)R (E = P, R = Me, OMe, Ph; E = As, R = Me) afford only trans-[Pt(Mef){OC(=CHEPh₃)R}(PPh₃)₂] because the C-alkyl/C-ylide transphobia is greater than the C-alkyl/O-ylide transphobia and also because of the lower steric requirement of the O-ylide ligand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f3e9240-a7d9-4a4d-bc8d-7f3085bc82c2",
                                                "sense_id": "bf4d39d4-1922-3fd4-bcef-60d11145036c",
                                                "text": "In the symbiotic effect, a hard ligand tends to form ionic M-L bonds in which L retains more negative charge than in a soft ligand case, letting the metal ion keep more of its positive charge and hence attract additional hard ligands, […]. The antisymbiotic effect, also called transphobia, applies to pairs of high trans effect, soft ligands on a soft metal. Where a choice exists, there is a strong tendency for such ligands to avoid being mutually trans by becoming cis and preferring to have low trans effect, hard ligands trans to themselves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0146d4f0-b492-498f-9257-6a6e7b076848",
                        "source_entry_id": "49846f81-265f-3a4a-92d9-f49dd9f38bdf",
                        "source_sense_id": "413c2e51-26a3-3540-b479-ba724c2637d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "transfobie",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "09a68bde-2f78-4b90-8092-289d6632332d",
                        "source_entry_id": "49846f81-265f-3a4a-92d9-f49dd9f38bdf",
                        "source_sense_id": "413c2e51-26a3-3540-b479-ba724c2637d7",
                        "target_lang_word": "transphobie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "transphobie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "699fc0de-40a7-34b7-a601-3a507d97e4f7",
                                        "entry_id": "12ab4f52-fbee-331e-86bb-8b283abee5b6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Discrimination, aversion envers la transidentité ou comportement hostile à l’égard des personnes transgenres ou transsexuelles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Transitude"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d2e96a7-25f6-452c-9ede-fbc1851242b7",
                                                "sense_id": "699fc0de-40a7-34b7-a601-3a507d97e4f7",
                                                "text": "Dans l’esprit du texte, les discriminations transphobes seraient incluses dans l’homophobie. Nous pensons néanmoins qu’il serait bien préférable de mentionner la transphobie comme une discrimination spécifique. Ce point semble loin d'être acquis."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11d5a69f-b0fe-49c7-a390-39041b811376",
                                                "sense_id": "699fc0de-40a7-34b7-a601-3a507d97e4f7",
                                                "text": "« Pour ce 17 mai 2010 nous constatons un progrès mais la lutte contre l’homophobie et la transphobie est un combat quotidien dans lequel tous les acteurs professionnels doivent s’impliquer », ajoutent les associations, qui organisent plusieurs actions à cette occasion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56bb61a9-95e1-49fe-9ee7-787e7f2aaad3",
                                                "sense_id": "699fc0de-40a7-34b7-a601-3a507d97e4f7",
                                                "text": "Cette hypocrisie professionnelle n'est pas réductible au seul contre-transfert. l s'agit d'une véritable hostilité à l'égard des patients, liée à un rejet moral de la même nature que le racisme, et qui porte aujourd'hui un nom: la transphobie. Les manquements éthiques de ces thérapeutes qui continuent de recevoir des sujets transsexuels en parfaite connaissance de cause eu égard à leur hostilité sont gravissimes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7174ab2-a9ce-4fb1-adf1-2bbb9953ee6a",
                                                "sense_id": "699fc0de-40a7-34b7-a601-3a507d97e4f7",
                                                "text": "Mais il faudrait distinguer un autre type de transphobie, \"institutionnelle\", celle-ci, et qui, en limitant l'accès au changement d'état civil et aux opérations remboursées, rend vulnérables l'ensemble des personnes souhaitant transitionner selon leurs propres modes de transition (chirurgicale, hormonale, nominale, etc.)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
